1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:03,801
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:03,801 --> 00:00:07,396
I remember your parents' first house very well.

3
00:00:07,396 --> 00:00:09,210
It was on Spring Avenue, near the park.

4
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:10,866
I grew up in that house.

5
00:00:10,866 --> 00:00:13,579
Yes, and you were such a cute baby.

6
00:00:13,579 --> 00:00:15,265
I've seen pictures of him.

7
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:16,765
He had blond hair.

8
00:00:16,765 --> 00:00:19,345
I've been friendly with the Stewart family

9
00:00:19,345 --> 00:00:20,822
for a long time,

10
00:00:20,822 --> 00:00:22,299
so it's my pleasure

11
00:00:22,299 --> 00:00:22,526
to help you find a house now.

12
00:00:22,526 --> 00:00:24,411
Well, we're not sure we can afford one.

13
00:00:24,411 --> 00:00:26,171
But we'd like to find out

14
00:00:26,171 --> 00:00:27,373
about the possibilities.

15
00:00:27,373 --> 00:00:28,516
That's a good idea.

16
00:00:28,516 --> 00:00:32,030
I love your house on Linden Street.

17
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:35,305
I sold your father that house seventeen years ago.

18
00:00:35,305 --> 00:00:35,531
Really?

19
00:00:35,531 --> 00:00:37,394
Yes, Mom was pregnant with Robbie then,

20
00:00:37,394 --> 00:00:39,098
and they needed the extra room.

21
00:00:39,098 --> 00:00:41,530
I hear you're expecting a baby, Mrs. Stewart.

22
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:42,239
Mmm-hmm.

23
00:00:42,239 --> 00:00:46,065
So we will be needing more room.

24
00:00:46,065 --> 00:00:46,383
Oh, so you don't need something immediately?

25
00:00:46,383 --> 00:00:50,625
No. But in five or six months ...

26
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:52,292
And time passes so quickly.

27
00:00:52,292 --> 00:00:53,292
Yes, it does.

28
00:00:53,292 --> 00:00:54,503
Well, when you called,

29
00:00:54,503 --> 00:00:56,003
you gave me enough information

30
00:00:56,003 --> 00:00:56,581
about your salaries and your savings.

31
00:00:56,581 --> 00:00:59,559
So I have a good idea about your financial situation.

32
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:02,872
Let me show you some pictures of houses.

33
00:01:02,872 --> 00:01:03,877
With two bedrooms?

34
00:01:03,877 --> 00:01:06,052
Yes, I think I can show you some.

35
00:01:06,052 --> 00:01:07,715
Of course, they won't be in Riverdale.

36
00:01:07,715 --> 00:01:10,493
The cost of housing's too high for you here.

37
00:01:10,493 --> 00:01:12,971
I haven't thought about living anywhere else.

38
00:01:12,971 --> 00:01:16,129
We've always lived in this area.

39
00:01:16,129 --> 00:01:18,157
Where should we look for a house, Mrs. Martinelli?

40
00:01:18,157 --> 00:01:20,104
Well, we have an office in Mount Kisco.

41
00:01:20,104 --> 00:01:21,190
It's a lovely area,

42
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:24,003
and it's only about an hour's drive from here.

43
00:01:24,003 --> 00:01:24,623
Here.

44
00:01:24,623 --> 00:01:28,361
I have a book with photos of some homes in that area.

45
00:01:28,361 --> 00:01:35,670
Now, let's see. Here.

46
00:01:35,670 --> 00:01:41,251
This is a lovely two-bedroom house in your price range.

47
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:48,751
It's pretty,

48
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:48,951
but I prefer a two-story home.

49
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:48,951
I do, too.

50
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:48,951
I don't care for a ranch type.

51
00:01:48,887 --> 00:01:50,185
OK.

52
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,463
Oh, this is a wonderful house.

53
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:54,663
I know it well.

54
00:01:54,663 --> 00:01:56,807
I sold it to the present owners.

55
00:01:56,807 --> 00:01:57,807
It looks wonderful.

56
00:01:57,807 --> 00:02:00,416
This is a two-bedroom, two-bath house.

57
00:02:00,416 --> 00:02:02,096
It has a full basement,

58
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:05,074
and it is on a half-acre lot.

59
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:07,611
You can probably afford this one.

60
00:02:07,611 --> 00:02:09,052
I like this house.

61
00:02:09,052 --> 00:02:10,052
So do I.

62
00:02:10,052 --> 00:02:11,474
And the price is right.

63
00:02:11,474 --> 00:02:13,030
Would you like to go see it?

64
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:14,470
Yes. We're planning

65
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:16,546
to talk to someone at the bank next week.

66
00:02:16,546 --> 00:02:18,986
Perhaps we could see the house this weekend.

67
00:02:18,986 --> 00:02:22,942
If someone doesn't buy it before then,

68
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:24,565
But let's keep looking.

69
00:02:24,565 --> 00:02:29,420
Just to get an idea of some other possibilities.

70
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:30,968
This is very helpful, Mrs. Martinelli.

71
00:02:30,968 --> 00:02:31,876
Here.

72
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:35,229
This is a wonderful example of Spanish-style architecture.

73
00:02:35,229 --> 00:02:35,604
Oh,

74
00:02:35,604 --> 00:02:40,152
I love the roof tiles on a Spanish-style house.

75
00:02:40,152 --> 00:02:42,442
It looks like the houses in Hollywood.

76
00:02:42,442 --> 00:02:43,788
It's interesting.

77
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:55,700
A house like this in Riverdale costs double the price.

78
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,678
Oh my!

79
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,656
Here's a real buy.

80
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:03,156
It's a bargain.

81
00:03:03,156 --> 00:03:06,234
This house just came on the market.

82
00:03:06,234 --> 00:03:07,612
It's quite lovely.

83
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:09,392
Is it a two-bedroom house?

84
00:03:09,392 --> 00:03:11,781
No. It has three bedrooms and three baths.

85
00:03:11,781 --> 00:03:12,973
I know the house.

86
00:03:12,973 --> 00:03:14,658
It has a brand new kitchen.

87
00:03:14,658 --> 00:03:17,212
And a living room with a twelve-foot ceiling.

88
00:03:17,212 --> 00:03:19,212
And there's a two-car garage.

89
00:03:19,212 --> 00:03:21,523
Then why don't we go look at this house, too?

90
00:03:21,523 --> 00:03:24,641
It's a good investment.

91
00:03:24,641 --> 00:03:25,479
Thank you, Mrs. Martinelli.

92
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:26,679
Thanks so much.

93
00:03:26,679 --> 00:03:28,743
My pleasure.

94
00:03:28,743 --> 00:03:30,457
Give my best to your parents.

95
00:03:30,457 --> 00:03:32,253
Your father's a wonderful doctor, Richard.

96
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:33,890
He took care of my daughter

97
00:03:33,890 --> 00:03:44,413
when she was a child.

98
00:03:44,413 --> 00:03:44,613
He's the best pediatrician in Westchester.

99
00:03:44,413 --> 00:03:44,613
Thanks, Mrs. Martinelli.

100
00:03:44,413 --> 00:03:44,613
I'll give them your regards.

101
00:03:44,413 --> 00:03:44,613
We really appreciate your advice.

102
00:03:44,413 --> 00:03:44,922
I do think you should go see the houses

103
00:03:44,922 --> 00:03:46,325
and talk to the bank.

104
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:46,565
Here.

105
00:03:46,565 --> 00:03:49,303
Let me give you some information sheets about the houses.

106
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:56,486
They're both very good buys.

107
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:59,237
Well, thanks so much for your help and your time,

108
00:03:59,237 --> 00:03:59,737
Mrs. Martinelli.

109
00:03:59,737 --> 00:04:02,644
We've got a lot to talk about.

110
00:04:02,644 --> 00:04:05,644
Mmm-hmm. Thanks.
